                <pb facs="0579" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg459"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/827: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sterling</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-27T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                                1922—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 1:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2. The Minister for Foreign Affairs is ready to withdraw the reply of the
                    Peruvian Government, the translation of which was sent to you in my 96, January
                    19, 7 p.m. and to replace it with another one in the exact terms of the first
                    note but omitting the words “ajustado por el gobierno de los Estados Unidos
                    (adjusted by the Government of the United States).” Is this satisfactory? Rush
                    reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
